hat":"Reads rows from an Airtable base or adds new records — like a smarter spreadsheet","overview":"List, get, create, update, upsert, and delete Airtable records. The resource dropdown is visual only; runtime implements record operations, not table-management APIs.","tips":["Use a Personal Access Token with data.records scopes or a saved Airtable connection","Base ID plus table/tableId are required for every operation","Create/update/upsert return records/count","Upsert also returns created and updated counts","Delete returns deletedRecords/count, not top-level deleted:true"],"docsHref":"/docs/nodes/airtable","why":"Prevents the same appointment reminder being sent again on the next scheduled run."}}}]$tpl$::jsonb,
